From b1f6df00720a0e166e5191ca7c850efbebf7a7db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:05:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] raptor: a detection settings page and a labelled preview
 overlay

raptor's IVS detection could be set in raptor.conf alone, and what it found
showed only as rod's unlabelled boxes in the sub stream.

- config-detect.html (Settings > Detection), installed with the IVS build
  option: on and off, the method (the ones whose libraries the image has),
  sensitivity and cooldown, and for a model its file, class count, confidence
  and overlap. A save writes only what changed; when the camera stages a
  setting for a restart, the page offers it. With no model on the camera the
  page says so.
- The preview gets a Detections button: boxes with the class name and score
  over the picture, for the viewer alone, fed by json-detect.cgi as one
  server-sent event stream while it is on; no boxes are drawn over a player
  without a picture.
- detect-overlay.js draws for both detectors: thingino-ipud's overlay was the
  same code, so preview-ipud.js now only feeds it from its own event stream.
  Same button, same remembered choice.

The overlay and its feed have run on an Ingenic T31 camera with detection
on, the boxes following at a median of 360 ms; the page scripts pass a host
test of 46 checks. The two raptor patches that let rod's boxes reach the sub
stream at all are 0112 and 0113 of the Thingino series.
